K1 opens a dedicated manually assigned guarded consumer from a copied credential configuration; auto commit is disabled by the existing factory, group/static membership removed, offset reset forbidden, one-record poll and frame/Fetch/timeouts bounded. Authenticated Fetch proof and exact source offset/timestamp/leader epoch plus Reference full envelope/Owner/locator/budget must match. It has no offset commit or physical send path.
P1 opens an owned Exclusive NonDurable guarded cursor with inclusive reset and queue size one. Async opening/seek/receive/proof/image work uses a deadline; any late-created cursor after timeout is closed. Stable post-seek and unchanged after-receive proof are mandatory. Source/batch identity and full signed bytes must match. No active consumer ACK is called; successful return also requires owned cursor close confirmation. The current proof helper is shared package-locally, not replaced by unguarded Reader API.

Both require an explicit caller history guard for protected retention and credential/Owner lifetime before/after native I/O. A successful read is not SEND/GC/long-term retention/production authority. Broker absence/gaps, resource or frame mismatch and timeout fail closed, preserving the external recovery obligation.

